  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed L-shaped rear dormer roof extension, by reason of its excessive scale, massing, and failure to maintain the mandatory 500mm separation distances from the main roof ridge, eaves, and side boundaries, results in an overly bulky and dominant addition that fails to appear visually subordinate to the host dwelling. Consequently, and owing to its clear visibility from Rosebery Avenue, the development would result in a highly conspicuous and incongruous feature that causes significant harm to the visual amenity of the street scene and the architectural character of the original building, contrary to Policy D3 of the London Plan (2021), Policies CS8 and DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012), Policy Guidance 26 and 39 of the Kingston Residential Design SPD (2013), and the design principles of the National Planning Policy Framework\r"
